p  having to wait a really long time the  goal of this competition is to design  and draw a boss and the only requirement  really is that your inspiration must be  drawn from the folklore that Elden ring  is rumored to be inspired by it  so that's Scandinavian Nordic folklore  Gaelic folklore Irish folklore Celtic  mythology or even Scottish mythology of  course Elden ring might not end up  inspired by these things at all but it's  a start  and all of these places have incredible  creatures and themes and stories and  whether you choose just one of these  sources or a mixture for your boss  design is up to you in the description  I've listed some reading material to  sort of start you off but I encourage  you to go beyond this and look on your  own as well once you've chosen your  inspiration and you've drawn your piece  send it to me with a bit of a written  description two things I'd like you to  write in your email first tell me what  folklore that you were actually inspired  by and second tell me a little bit about  your boss fight tell me for example  what's its name  where does the fight take place does the  fight have dialog does it have phases  law does the boss have weaknesses does  it make use of the open world in some  way if you decide to draw a background  environment is this where the fight  takes place just give me some  information don't worry about answering  all these questions I just want you to  give me some idea of what the fight is  like and how it reflects your boss  design if you're still looking for more  inspiration bear in mind that I have two  videos on Eldon Ring now there's a  cinematic where two characters in it  have sort of prosthetic arms there's two  knights in this trailer that have red  hair they're all high fantasy styled  Knights these are all sort of trends  that you can maybe pull inspiration from  as well so go watch the trailer go watch  my videos he'll go on the Eldon Ring  subreddit and look at some of the bosses  that people have just made up and posted  about I'm sure these people would be ok  with you bringing their ideas to life as  long as you credit them in your email  I've linked some really good comments  from the subreddit down below assuming  this contest goes well at least the top  10 winners will be featured in a video  and there will be special mention to  other contestants as well prize  distribution is as follows on screen and  it will be delivered via PayPal you have  until midnight on the 23rd of November  PST to email your art to Eldon ring  challenge at gmail.com remember twinks  a written description of the folklore  you were inspired by tell me how the  bossfight works list your artist  portfolio social media and also your  paypal address in case you win if you  have any questions don't email them  instead head over to my discord and go  to the Eldon Ring FAQ and see if your  question has already been asked if it  hasn't you can ask the question in the  text channel below it thank you so much  for your interest I think this is gonna  be fun if you're not an artist maybe  share this competition with an artist  that you know and good luck see you in a  month
 

